<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12829" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποκινδυν-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make a desperate venture, try a forlorn hope,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τινα</span>
			<i>against</i> another, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.81
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ τῶν εὐτυχούντων ἦν τὸ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					159
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἔν τινι</span>
			<i>to make trial in</i> his <i>case, upon</i> him, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				4.2.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				2.104
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πάσαις ταῖς δυνάμεσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					3.52
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. περὶ τῶν ὅλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Alex.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. cogn., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τοῦτο</span>
			<i>to make</i> this <i>venture,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				4.17
			</span></i>: c. inf., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποκινδυνεύετον . . σοφόν τι λέγειν</span> Ar <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ra.</u>
				1108
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμῖν . . ἀποκεκινδυνεύσεται τὰ χρήματα</span>”
				<i>will be put to the uttermost hazard,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.39
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>shrink from the dangers of</i> another, <i>abandon</i> him
				<i>in danger,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
				</span></i>
			<i>V A</i><i><span class="en">
				7.15
			</span></i>.</div>
